(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609112107-reservation-cljk-host-loader-contract")
  (:adr/topic "cljk-host-loader")
  (:adr/title "Opt-in managed canonical cljk host source patch and qualification")
  (:adr/status "proposed")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/body "Implementation proposal: scripts/nbb-cljk now contains a source patch and dependency lock for fixed upstream babashka/nbb 4fff82ea9bb74ae0f49d5c8fed5723f2eee71445 (v1.4.208). The patch extends find-file-on-classpath and load-file validation; it does not patch compiled JavaScript or copy canonical sources under other suffixes. The existing root nbb command is unchanged. New opt-in npm run nbb:cljk selects a separately rebuilt task-local cache. NBB_CLJK_ROOTS or explicit config :cljk-roots registers repository ownership and origin manifests, propagating to existing child process entrypoints.\n\nThe source resolver preserves classpath order, uses declared .cljs then .cljc platform preference, and rejects unknown/ambiguous/target-incompatible candidates, duplicate manifest keys and paths escaping registered repositories. It resolves transitive require/reload through the existing host path and re-reads manifests. Tests cover original source error paths and legacy compatibility. Full contract and exact reproduction commands live in scripts/nbb-cljk/README.md; build-manifest.json records fixed upstream, patch/lock and artifact hashes.\n\nQualification: built with upstream shadow-cljs release (advanced) and compiled test modules. Loader conformance: 7 tests / 23 assertions passed. Upstream unit tests with opt-in unset: 46 tests / 79 assertions passed. Canonical original source node unit tests: 33/106; archive: 7/39; ref_race: seven witness processes, exactly one winner and one loser, all witnesses agree, invalid proof rejected; run: disposable identity, local health response and process termination. No source mirror participates. Tests use explicit source classpaths; normal archive dependency pin integration remains pending merged inga.\n\nStatus stays proposed and PR stays Draft: this is an implemented, locally qualified compatibility patch, not fleet adoption or production deployment. Root global installation/shared checkout is unchanged. No upstream fork release, unmerged dependency pin, production credential or live money movement. Review order: managed loader patch; inga https://github.com/kotoba-lang/inga/pull/15; archive https://github.com/kotoba-lang/inga-node/pull/3 dependency integration against merged inga. Review and fleet acceptance remain distinct from these local results.")
))
